WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.970
About 80 per cent of the
world's goods move by sea.

2
00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:07.350
Narrow chokepoints, such as
the Suez and Panama canals,

3
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.530
concentrate those flows.

4
00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:16.630
By late January 2024, trade through Suez
had fallen by 42 per cent in two months.

5
00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:20.990
Panama Canal transits were down
36 per cent on a year earlier.

6
00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:23.410
Two canals on opposite sides of the world,

7
00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.310
faltering at once.

8
00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:27.130
Did one storm hit both?

9
00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:28.980
A single cyberattack?

10
00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:33.830
In this mission, you'll sort
supply-chain risks into three kinds:

11
00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:36.330
political, economic and physical.

12
00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:41.870
Then you'll follow shocks from Thailand's
2011 floods to a global chip shortage.

13
00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:46.650
Your mission: explain why two canals on
opposite sides of the world faltered at

14
00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:47.390
once.
